Feature: Validate delivery_dt Datatype and Format in f_order Table

  Background:
    Given the f_order table exists in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" under schema "purgo_playground"
    And the SQL script is located at "/Workspace/stg/scripts/f_order.sql"

  Scenario: Successful validation of delivery_dt as Decimal(38,0) in yyyymmdd format
    Given the f_order table contains a delivery_dt value "20240910"
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then the delivery_dt "20240910" should be recognized as Decimal(38,0)
    And the format of delivery_dt should match "yyyyMMdd"
    And no validation errors should be reported

  Scenario Outline: Validation failure due to incorrect delivery_dt datatype or format
    Given the f_order table contains a delivery_dt value "<delivery_dt>"
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then the delivery_dt "<delivery_dt>" should fail validation
    And the error message should be "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | delivery_dt | error_message                                    |
      | 2024-09-10  | delivery_dt is not Decimal(38,0)                  |
      | 20240931    | delivery_dt does not represent a valid date       |
      | 20240000    | delivery_dt does not represent a valid date       |
      | 20241301    | delivery_dt does not represent a valid date       |
      | 2024091     | delivery_dt is not in yyyymmdd format             |
      | 2024091001  | delivery_dt is not in yyyymmdd format             |
      | -20240910   | delivery_dt must be a positive Decimal(38,0) value|

  Scenario: All delivery_dt values pass validation
    Given the f_order table is populated with valid delivery_dt values in yyyymmdd format as Decimal(38,0)
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then all delivery_dt values should pass the Decimal(38,0) and yyyymmdd format checks
    And no validation errors should be reported

  Scenario: Some delivery_dt values have incorrect Decimal(38,0) datatype
    Given the f_order table contains both valid and invalid delivery_dt values
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then only the invalid delivery_dt values should fail the Decimal(38,0) check
    And appropriate error messages should be logged for each failure

  Scenario: Some delivery_dt values have incorrect yyyymmdd format
    Given the f_order table contains delivery_dt values with incorrect formatting
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then only the improperly formatted delivery_dt values should fail the yyyymmdd format check
    And appropriate error messages should be logged for each failure

  Scenario: Execution triggers and reporting
    Given the SQL validation logic is scheduled to run daily
    When the SQL job executes
    Then the validation results should be logged in the reporting system
    And any failures should trigger an alert with the corresponding error messages

  Scenario: Performance constraints during validation
    Given the f_order table contains a large volume of records
    When the SQL validation logic is executed
    Then the validation should complete within the specified performance thresholds
    And resource utilization should remain within acceptable limits
